    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.keymap\n\n### Description\n\nCurrently, the built-in jump steps in `mini.keymap`:\n- `jump_after_close`\n- `jump_before_open`\n\nonly work in *insert* mode.\n\nIt would be great if these also worked in command-line mode for consistency between modes, especially when used alongside `mini.pairs`, which already supports command-line editing. This would make jumping over paired delimiters feel seamless whether you’re typing in insert or command mode.",
    "closed_at": "2025-11-12T09:44:31Z",
