        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I did a quick modification to the source to experiment with this and was able to get the desired behavior in command-line mode:\n\n```lua\nH.steps_builtin.jump_after_close_cmd = {\n  condition = function() return vim.fn.mode() == \"c\" end,\n  action = function()\n    local cmd = vim.fn.getcmdline()\n    local pos = vim.fn.getcmdpos()\n    local next = string.find(cmd, \"[%])}\\\"'`]\", pos)\n    if next then\n      local diff = next - pos + 1\n      local move = string.rep(\"<Right>\", diff)\n      vim.api.nvim_feedkeys(vim.api.nvim_replace_termcodes(move, true, false, true), \"c\", false)\n    end\n  end,\n}\n\nH.steps_builtin.jump_before_open_cmd = {\n  condition = function() return vim.fn.mode() == \"c\" end,\n  action = function()\n    local cmd = vim.fn.getcmdline()\n    local pos = vim.fn.getcmdpos()\n    local rev = cmd:sub(1, pos - 1):reverse()\n    local rev_index = rev:find(\"[%(%[{\\\"'`]\")\n    if not rev_index then return end\n    local match_pos = (pos - 1) - rev_index + 1\n    local diff = pos - match_pos\n    if diff > 0 then\n      local move = string.rep(\"<Left>\", diff)\n      vim.api.nvim_feedkeys(vim.api.nvim_replace_termcodes(move, true, false, true), \"c\", false)\n    end\n  end,\n}\n```\n\nThis works well in my testing so far, but I imagine it could be integrated more cleanly into the existing gen_step.search_pattern() helper or unified with the Insert-mode implementation for better maintainability.",
