        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nI don't think including Command-line mode implementations to built-in steps is a good idea. Mostly indeed because they are significantly different from how Insert mode actions are implemented. But also because for complex editing I'd recommend using `:h command-line-window`: press `<C-f>` when inside Command line and add/edit text in a very similar way to the normal buffer.\n\nClosing as not planned.\n\n---\n\nOne suggestion for the code solution posted: instead of `nvim_feedkeys()` with arrow keys, using `vim.fn.setcmdpos()` should be more straightforward.",
